    "narrative": "The clear headliner for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, boasting an elite 80.87 score. His matchup against Roki Sasaki is highlighted by the \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric, which significantly elevates his stolen base potential\u2014the primary currency of our strategy. Paired with a favorable #2 spot in the order and platoon advantages, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine for the day. **Brice Turang** (68.83) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.23) round out the top tier. **Brice Turang** benefits similarly from a slow opposing delivery, while **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a high-ceiling outing due to a strong 14% boost from his dynamic platoon split against the right-handed arm. \n\nThe optimizer\u2019s most difficult exclusion was **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 46.31 score. While his matchup against JT Brubaker offers a favorable SP_xERA, the combination of a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a defensive penalty against an elite-framing catcher suppressed his efficiency score just enough to keep him on the bench. We are also closely monitoring the weather in the **Austin Riley** game, as a 38% rain risk adds a layer of volatility to his 50.15 projection. Furthermore, with the lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Seiya Suzuki** still officially pending, our reliance on these assumed spots introduces a minor risk factor. We remain cautious regarding **Austin Riley** and his rain-shortened potential, keeping our depth pieces like **Cole Young** ready should any late lineup shifts necessitate a swap.",
